# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are recorded in this file.

## 2026-07-10 — 1.0.0 (major)

### First Stable Release

LOMO reaches version 1.0.0 — the ontology, SHACL shapes, tooling, and documentation are considered stable for production use.

#### SHACL Shapes

- Rewrote SHACL shapes: per-scheme validation, instance data shapes, moved to `shapes/` folder
- Fixed instance data to use correct vocabulary namespace URIs

#### Interoperability Assessment (IOPA)

- Added LFDS assessment serialisation and IOPA portal submission workflow
- Interoperability binding via 'all' + article↔paragraph coverage
- Project LOMO+IOPA assessments into IEP POST payloads
- Added `scripts/submit.py` for POSTing assessment payloads to the Interoperable Europe Portal
- Handle 'no barriers' assessments and PublicService description fallback
- Extract 4.4 assessment subtables and serialise as IOPA assessments
- Make LFDS assessments submission-shaped for the IOPA portal
- Asset description = name alignment
- Dropped `dctype:Software` → `adms:Asset` alignment axiom

#### Extraction Improvements

- Support the 'Policy domain' requirements-table variant
- Robust table classification recovers dropped LFDS tables
- Classify tables with a leading spanning/title row

#### Documentation

- Added project README

#### Maintenance

- Bumped ontology version to `1.0.0` and updated `dcterms:modified` to `2026-07-10`
- Bumped `pyproject.toml` version to `1.0.0`
- Removed outdated script

#### Files Changed

- `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` — version bump
- `shapes/lomo-shapes.ttl` — rewritten SHACL shapes
- `scripts/submit.py` — new IEP submission script
- `scripts/` — IOPA and extraction scripts updated
- `data/**/*.ttl` — instance data namespace fixes
- `pyproject.toml` — version bump
- `README.md` — new file

## 2026-07-09 — 0.8.2 (patch)

### Patch Release

This release migrates the ontology and vocabulary namespaces to their permanent URIs under `http://data.europa.eu/leg/`, fixes SHACL shapes consistency, and cleans up documentation and tooling.

#### Namespace Changes

- Updated ontology namespace from `http://data.europa.eu/lomo` to `http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo`
- Updated vocabulary namespaces from `http://data.europa.eu/lomo/ontologies/<name>` to `http://data.europa.eu/leg/<name>`:
  - `http://data.europa.eu/leg/deontic-modality#`
  - `http://data.europa.eu/leg/result-category#`
  - `http://data.europa.eu/leg/temporal-function#`
  - `http://data.europa.eu/leg/digital-dimensions#`
- Updated all SPARQL queries, Python scripts, instance data, and SHACL shapes to use new URIs

#### SHACL Shapes Fixes

- Fixed `sh:hasValue` URIs for `DeonticModality_inScheme`, `ResultCategory_inScheme`, `TemporalFunction_inScheme` to point to correct vocabulary namespaces
- Fixed `Concept_inScheme` `sh:in` list to use new vocabulary scheme URIs
- Removed stale "Constitutive Rule" from deontic modality label/prefLabel/comment/scopeNote enumerations
- Updated `DeonticModality_comment` values to match current `rdfs:comment` text
- Added trigger to `TemporalFunction_comment` enumeration
- Updated `ConceptScheme_comment` and `ConceptScheme_description` to include Digital Dimensions and correct counts
- Removed stale `hasTopConcept_class_2` and `hasTopConcept_class_4` referencing non-existent classes

#### Documentation & Tooling

- Fixed `vann:usageExample` strings in `lomo-ontology.ttl` and `result-category.ttl` to use correct vocabulary IRIs instead of stale `lomo:` prefix references
- Removed dead vocabulary import code from `run_queries.py`
- Removed dead query-rewriting regex logic from `run_queries.py`
- Simplified `controlled_vocabularies.rq` — removed obsolete `owl:intersectionOf` branch
- Removed internal/external distinction from controlled vocabularies HTML template

#### Maintenance

- Bumped ontology version to `0.8.2` and updated `dcterms:modified` to `2026-07-09`
- Bumped `pyproject.toml` version to `0.8.2`

#### Files Changed

- `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` — namespace, version bump, usageExample fixes
- `ontologies/deontic-modality.ttl` — namespace update
- `ontologies/digital-dimensions.ttl` — namespace update
- `ontologies/result-category.ttl` — namespace update, usageExample fix
- `ontologies/temporal-function.ttl` — namespace update
- `lomo-shapes.ttl` — namespace URIs fixed, stale enumerations corrected
- `sparql/*.rq` — namespace updates
- `scripts/queries/*.rq` — namespace updates
- `scripts/run_queries.py` — namespace updates, dead code removed
- `templates/partials/section-controlled-vocabularies.html` — removed internal/external labels
- `templates/partials/head.html` — fixed version URI to use `http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo/releases/`
- `data/**/*.ttl` — namespace updates in instance data
- `pyproject.toml` — version bump

## 2026-07-02 — 0.8.1 (patch)

### Patch Release

This release adds two new ConstitutiveRule subclasses, three new rule-to-rule relationship properties, restricts the permitted values of `lomo:withRole`, and improves object property documentation.

#### Ontology Enhancements

- **Issue #106**: Added `lomo:InstitutionalRule` as a subclass of `lomo:ConstitutiveRule` for provisions that establish institutional entities, legal statuses, powers, or organ composition
- **Issue #107**: Added `lomo:ScopeRule` as a subclass of `lomo:ConstitutiveRule` for provisions that define the material, personal, or territorial scope of application of a legal act
- **Issue #34**: Added defeasibility and rule-to-rule relationship properties:
  - `lomo:specifies` / `lomo:isSpecifiedBy` — for rules that determine underdetermined content of a more general rule without normative conflict
  - `lomo:derogatesFrom` / `lomo:isDerogatedBy` — for rules that establish an incompatible normative qualification, supporting substitutive and blocking derogations
  - `lomo:relatesTo` — super-property of both `specifies` and `derogatesFrom`, enabling generic querying across all rule-to-rule relationships
- **Issue #112**: Restricted `lomo:withRole` to three permitted OP AT Role concepts:
  - Added `owl:allValuesFrom` + `owl:oneOf` restriction on `lomo:AgentRole` enumerating `ADDRESSER`, `ADDRESSEE`, `BENEF`
  - Added `skos:scopeNote` on `lomo:withRole` documenting the restriction and its rationale
  - Added `:LomoPermittedRoles` `skos:Collection` grouping the three permitted concepts
  - Updated `vann:usageExample` on `lomo:AgentRole` to reference canonical AT Role URIs

#### Documentation & Query Improvements

- Updated object property SPARQL query and HTML template to expose sub-property and inverse-of relationships in the generated documentation

#### Maintenance

- Bumped ontology version to `0.8.1` and updated `dcterms:modified` to `2026-07-02`
- Updated `diagram-layout.json` with revised diagram layout
- Updated `.gitignore`
- Added `sh:in` constraint in `lomo-shapes.ttl` (`shapes:AgentRole_withRole`) enforcing the `withRole` restriction at SHACL validation level

#### Files Changed

- `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` — InstitutionalRule, ScopeRule, defeasibility properties, withRole restriction, version bump
- `lomo-shapes.ttl` — New `shapes:AgentRole` node shape with `sh:in` constraint on `lomo:withRole`
- `sparql/object_properties.rq` — Added sub-property and inverse-of to query
- `templates/partials/section-object-properties.html` — Display sub-property and inverse-of relationships
- `diagram-layout.json` — Updated layout
- `.gitignore` — Minor update

## 2026-06-15 — 0.8.0 (minor)

### Minor Release

This release introduces the splitting of SKOS controlled vocabularies into separate files and treats them as external authority tables in the documentation. It also adds various examples to classes and properties.

#### Ontology Enhancements

- **Issue #79**: Updated ActionResult example from EU 2024/1350
- **Issue #80**: Added examples for ActionResultType class
- **Issue #110**: Added skos:example and vann:usageExample to LegalRule
- **SKOS Vocabulary Splitting**:
  - Split DeonticModalityScheme into separate file `ontologies/deontic-modality.ttl`
  - Split TemporalFunctionScheme into separate file `ontologies/temporal-function.ttl`
  - Split ResultCategoryScheme into separate file `ontologies/result-category.ttl`
  - Split DigitalDimensionsScheme into separate file `ontologies/digital-dimensions.ttl`
  - Each vocabulary file now uses its own namespace (e.g., `http://data.europa.eu/lomo/ontologies/deontic-modality#`)
  - Updated properties to reference these external vocabularies via `rdfs:seeAlso` instead of `rdfs:range` with `owl:hasValue`
  - Removed `owl:imports` statements for these local vocabularies
- **Issue #109**: Replaced outdated Constitutive Rule examples and removed TFEU-based example

#### Documentation & Query Improvements

- **Controlled Vocabularies**: Split vocabularies now appear as external authority tables instead of internal concept schemes
- **Concepts Section**: Removed empty Concepts section from documentation templates
- Updated all template partials to use correct section indices after removing concepts section

#### Maintenance

- Bumped ontology version to `0.8.0` and updated `dcterms:modified` to `2026-06-15`
- Updated version references in ontology metadata

#### Files Changed

- `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` — Property updates, namespace changes, examples added
- `ontologies/deontic-modality.ttl` — New file with DeonticModalityScheme
- `ontologies/temporal-function.ttl` — New file with TemporalFunctionScheme
- `ontologies/result-category.ttl` — New file with ResultCategoryScheme
- `ontologies/digital-dimensions.ttl` — New file with DigitalDimensionsScheme
- `sparql/concepts.rq` — Deleted (no longer needed)
- `scripts/run_queries.py` — Updated query_map and section count
- `templates/main.html` — Removed section-concepts reference
- `templates/partials/section-concepts.html` — Deleted
- `templates/partials/section-controlled-vocabularies.html` — Updated section index
- `templates/partials/section-object-properties.html` — Updated section index
- `templates/partials/section-datatype-properties.html` — Updated section index

