## 2026-01-16 — 0.6.0 (minor)

### Modelling changes

- **Renames:** Renamed core ontology classes:
  - `:LegalInformationObject` → `:LegalRule` (root class for legal fragments)
  - `:LegalRequirement` → `:PrescriptiveRule` (prescriptive norms that carry deontic modalities)

- **Property domain/range adjustments:** Properties whose domain previously referenced `:LegalRequirement` or `:LegalInformationObject` were updated to use `:PrescriptiveRule` or `:LegalRule` respectively (examples include `:hasDeonticModality`, `:produces`, `:hasRequirementType`, `:hasCategory`, `:references`, and domain/range clarifications for `:establishedInResource`).

### Changes since 0.5.4

 - `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` — renames and modelling refactor described above (class renames, domain/range updates, scope note clarifications).
 - `pyproject.toml` — packaging version bump to `0.6.0`.

If you want, I can add a more detailed, per-commit list or paste the git diff showing the exact lines changed in `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl`.

## 2026-01-16 — 0.5.4 (patch)

### Ontology Editorial Fixes

- **Metadata bump:** `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` version updated to `0.6.4` and `dcterms:modified` set to `2026-01-16`.
- **Editorial & reorganisation changes:** The file contains a number of editorial corrections, wording clarifications, and a reorganisation of the controlled-vocabulary individuals and SKOS concept-scheme blocks (several scheme/individual blocks were moved toward the end of the file under a consolidated "Individuals - Controlled vocabularies" section).
- **IRI adjustments:** The `cdm:` prefix declaration was removed and CDM IRIs are now used inline (replaced with the full CDM IRI `<http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/cdm#...>` where required).
- **Property and wording refinements:** Small refinements to property comments and scope notes (examples: `:atTime`, `:hasFrequency`, `:overlaps`, `:hasResult` and `:Frequency` wording changes).

### Documentation & Tooling

- **SPARQL & Documentation queries:** Added a controlled-vocabularies query and more comprehensive ontology metadata extraction to support richer generated documentation (`sparql/controlled_vocabularies.rq`, `sparql/ontology_metadata.rq`). Updated `summary.md` to include generated summaries.
- **Documentation generator enhancements:** Improved `scripts/run_queries.py` to implement HTML annotation and citation features, simplify and refactor annotation helpers (including `annotate_see_also_html`), and make the output more robust for the template renderer.
- **Template improvements:** Multiple updates to `template-vocbench.html` to improve structure and rendering compatibility with the enhanced query outputs and annotations.
- **Packaging / build config:** Updated project packaging and build metadata (`pyproject.toml`, `poetry.toml`, `poetry.lock`) to support the documentation build and new dependencies.
- **Tests:** Updated `tests/test_references.py` to reflect changes in annotation output and template rendering.

## 2026-01-15 — 0.5.3 (patch)

### Ontology Maintenance

- **Rename root fragment class:** Renamed the LOMO-native root class `:LegalFragment` to `:LegalInformationObject` (symbol `:LegalInformationObject`), and updated labels, comments and scope notes accordingly to use the new human-readable name "Legal Information Object".
- **Established resource mapping:** Removed the `owl:equivalentClass cdm:fragment_resource_legal` statement from the root class and instead added the CDM fragment class (`cdm:fragment_resource_legal`) as part of the `:establishedInResource` property's range (union with `<http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#LegalResource>`). This keeps the ontology's internal class name cleaner while preserving CDM mapping on provenance links.
- **Subclass updates:** Updated `:LegalRequirement` and `:ConstitutiveRule` to be `rdfs:subClassOf :LegalInformationObject` and adjusted related scope notes and examples.
- **Removed `:setDefinition`:** Deleted the `:setDefinition` property (used previously to link fragments to their internal Definition instances). Replaced with guidance that `:Definition` instances are modeled as a subclass of `:ConstitutiveRule` and that applications should use `:usesDefinition` or project-specific containment patterns where appropriate.
- **Documentation updates:** Updated `skos:scopeNote` and other explanatory text throughout `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` to reflect the rename and the `:setDefinition` removal.

### Files Modified
- `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` — renamed root class, adjusted `:establishedInResource` range, removed `:setDefinition`, updated scope notes and subclass references.


## 2026-01-14 — 0.5.2 (patch)

### Ontology Enhancements

- **Digital Dimensions Integration**: Integrated LFDS Digital Dimensions classification into main ontology
  - Added `DigitalDimension` class as a subclass of `skos:Concept` with owl:equivalentClass restriction
  - Added `DigitalDimensionsScheme` SKOS concept scheme for digital dimension categories
  - Added four digital dimension concepts:
    - `Data`: Requirements related to data collection, transmission, storage, quality, and reuse
    - `Observation`: Discrete data points, measurements, rates, and thresholds (narrower concept of Data)
    - `DigitalPublicService`: Requirements related to digital public services
    - `DigitalSolutions`: Requirements related to digital infrastructure and software systems
  - Updated `:hasCategory` property with proper domain (`LegalRequirement`) and range (`DigitalDimension`)
  - Removed separate `lomo-digital-dimensions.ttl` file (now integrated into main ontology)

### Metadata & Documentation

- **Ontology Metadata**: Added `dcterms:editor` property to ontology metadata
- **ReSpec Configuration**: Fixed W3C ReSpec validation errors in documentation template
  - Changed `specStatus` from "WD" to "base"
  - Added `group: "base"` configuration option
  - Ensures proper W3C group association for documentation

### Files Modified
- `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl`: Version bumped to 0.5.2, digital dimensions integrated
- `template-vocbench.html`: ReSpec configuration updated

### Files Removed
- `ontologies/lomo-digital-dimensions.ttl`: Content integrated into main ontology

## 2026-01-14 — 0.5.1 (patch)

### Infrastructure & Documentation

- **CI/CD Pipeline**: Added automated documentation generation to `.gitlab-ci.yml`
  - New `build` stage that installs dependencies from `requirements.txt`
  - Automatically runs `scripts/run_queries.py` to generate fresh documentation
  - Deploys generated `lomo-docs.html` to GitLab Pages
  
- **Documentation Generation System**: Implemented automated SPARQL-based documentation generation
  - Added `scripts/run_queries.py`: Python script that queries the ontology and generates HTML documentation
  - Added `template-vocbench.html`: VocBench-compatible Mustache template for documentation rendering
  - Added 7 SPARQL query files in `sparql/` directory:
    - `ontology_metadata.rq`: Extracts ontology metadata
    - `authors.rq` & `editors.rq`: Extracts contributor information
    - `classes.rq`: Extracts class definitions and descriptions
    - `concepts.rq`: Extracts SKOS concept scheme information
    - `object_properties.rq` & `datatype_properties.rq`: Extracts property definitions
  - Added `requirements.txt`: Python dependencies (rdflib, chevron, pyparsing)

- **Ontology Updates**:
  - Declared controlled vocabulary classes as subclasses of `skos:Concept`
  - Added SKOS ontology import for proper vocabulary management
  - Declared formal equivalence between `DeonticModality` class and `DeonticModalityScheme`
  - Removed `owl:imports` of ELI ontology (resolving technical issues)

- **Repository Maintenance**:
  - Updated `.gitignore` to exclude generated files (`output_queries.json`, `lomo-docs.html`)
  - Code structure refactored for improved readability and maintainability

### Files Modified
- `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `.gitignore`, `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl`, `lomo-docs.html` (regenerated)

### Files Added
- `scripts/run_queries.py`, `template-vocbench.html`, `requirements.txt`
- `sparql/*.rq` (7 query files)

## 2026-01-14 — 0.5.0 (minor)

### Breaking Changes — Class Hierarchy Restructuring

This release introduces a significant restructuring of the ontology to resolve conceptual conflicts where `LegalRequirement` was too broad, `ConstitutiveRule` was mis-classified as a deontic modality, and `Definition` was incorrectly positioned in the hierarchy.

#### New Class: `LegalFragment`
- Added `:LegalFragment` as the LOMO-native root class for all legal fragments.
- Declared `owl:equivalentClass` to both `cdm:fragment_resource_legal` (Common Data Model) and `eli:LegalInformationObject` (ELI-LO), ensuring interoperability while allowing LOMO to be used independently.
- Added `cdm:` prefix for `http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/cdm#`.

#### Restructured Class Hierarchy
```
:LegalFragment (root - any legal fragment)
├── :LegalRequirement (prescriptive rules with deontic modalities)
└── :ConstitutiveRule (constitutive facts and definitions)
    └── :Definition (specialized constitutive rule)
```

#### `LegalRequirement` Restricted to Prescriptive Rules
- Now `rdfs:subClassOf :LegalFragment` (previously `owl:Thing`).
- Updated definition to clarify it only covers norms that prescribe actions (obligation, permission, prohibition, right).
- Aligned with ELI-LO's `LegalNorm` concept.

#### `ConstitutiveRule` Converted from Modality to Class
- Changed from `owl:NamedIndividual, :DeonticModality, skos:Concept` to `owl:Class`.
- Now `rdfs:subClassOf :LegalFragment`.
- Added `owl:disjointWith :LegalRequirement`.
- **Removed from `DeonticModalityScheme`** — constitutive rules are NOT deontic modalities.

#### `Definition` Repositioned
- Now `rdfs:subClassOf :ConstitutiveRule` (previously `owl:Thing`).
- Correctly positioned as a specialized kind of constitutive rule.

#### `DeonticModalityScheme` Updated
- Removed `ConstitutiveRule` from top concepts.
- Now only includes: `Obligation`, `Permission`, `Prohibition`, `Right`.

#### Property Updates
- `:hasDeonticModality`: Clarified it only applies to `LegalRequirement`.
- `:produces`: Clarified it only applies to prescriptive rules.
- `:setDefinition`: Changed domain from `LegalRequirement` to `:LegalFragment`.
- `:establishedInResource`, `:legalText`: Added scope notes for all fragment types.

### Other Changes
- Bumped version to **0.5.0**. 
- Updated `owl:versionIRI` to `<http://data.europa.eu/lomo/ontology/0.5.0>`.
- Files modified: `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl`, `lomo-docs.html`.

## 2026-01-08 — 0.4.1 (patch)

- Bumped patch version to **0.4.1**. 
- Fixed incorrect `xml:` prefix mapping (now correctly points to `http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace`) in the ontology and instance files.
- Standardised temporal class name usage in LOMO to `:TemporalSpecification` and removed stray references to deprecated names.
- Corrected `:setDefinition` label (now "sets definition") and added `rdfs:domain :LegalRequirement`.
- Added machine-readable metadata to the ontology header: `owl:versionIRI` and `dcterms:license` (EUPL v1.2 reference).
- Files modified: `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl`, `data/antidumping-microdisks-lrmo-instances.ttl`, `data/financial-reporting-lrmo-instances.ttl`, `data/vehicle-registration-lrmo-instances.ttl`, `data/fisheries-lrmo-instances.ttl`.

## 2026-01-08 — 0.4.0 LOMO rename

- Renamed ontology from **LRMO** to **LOMO** (Legal Obligation Metadata Ontology).
- Updated ontology IRI/base to `http://data.europa.eu/lomo` and prefix to `lomo:`.
- Replaced occurrences of `lrmo:` with `lomo:` in `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl` (examples and metadata).
- Updated ontology metadata: title changed to "Legal Obligation Metadata Ontology (LOMO)" and creator updated accordingly.
- File modified: `ontologies/lomo-ontology.ttl`.

